# Forge3D example: anim golden film (Wave 3, gates G3d/G3e).
# A two-scene, 48-frame film at 24 fps (2 s) at 320x240, authored
# to pin the v3 film renderer end to end: resolved character
# action tracks, a camera track, a dissolve transition, and
# multi-figure frames.  Durations are fractional seconds chosen
# so every span lands on an exact frame count at 24 fps:
#   scene 1 "stage": 0.75 s walk+pan (18 f) + 0.417 s wave (10 f)
#                    = 28 frames
#   scene 2 "leap":  0.5 s jump (12 f) + 0.334 s smile (8 f)
#                    = 20 frames, opening with a dissolve whose
#                    0.333 s rounds to exactly 8 frames.
# The film header declares 320x240 and each scene line repeats
# `size 320 240`: the compiled scene spans carry their own size
# (the film header size does not propagate to them), and the
# engine sizes its framebuffer from the span.
# Pinned frame hashes + the whole-sequence digest live in
# docs/V4-GOLDENS.md; CI gates G3d/G3e enforce them.
# Build: bin/f3dc build examples/anim-golden.f3d
# Render: bin/engine3d build/anim-golden.timeline.json

film "Anim Golden" size 320 240 fps 24

scene "stage" size 320 240 background white
camera at 0 3 10 look 0 1 0
plane ground gray at 0 -2 0 size 16
cube bench red at 3 0 0 size 2
place bench-front at 1 0 2
character ada blue at -3 0 2 tall head round wears cap red

together
  ada walks to bench-front in 0.75 seconds ease smooth
  camera pans to bench in 0.75 seconds ease smooth
end
ada waves for 0.417 seconds

scene "leap" size 320 240 background white transition dissolve 0.333 seconds
camera at 0 3 10 look 0 1 0
plane ground gray at 0 -2 0 size 16
character ada blue at -1 0 2 tall head round wears cap red
character mira pink at 3 0 2 kid head round hair bun

together
  ada jumps for 0.5 seconds
  mira waves for 0.5 seconds
end
together
  ada smiles for 0.334 seconds
  mira waves for 0.334 seconds
end

render "output_render.ppm"
